<p>Most of the players faster than Messi on this list are between 4 and 7 inches taller than him and weigh 20 to 35 pounds more. Physics dictates that longer legs generate more ground coverage per stride. Messi compensates for shorter stride length with an exceptional stride rate and the ability to maintain close to top speed through more rapid direction changes than any of these players can execute at their size.</p>
<p><strong>The more relevant number is his acceleration, not his top speed.</strong> Messi reportedly reaches close to maximum velocity within approximately 1.8 to 2.0 seconds from a standing start — among the fastest measured first-step accelerations in professional soccer. This is the metric that produces the separation you see on camera. He is past defenders before they register he has moved, not because he runs faster than them over 50 meters but because he accelerates to speed faster than they can react.</p>
